# @module tools.flow_cli.build
# @means  `flow run`, `compile`, `debug`, `shader`, `audio`, `window`,
#         `gfx`, `record`, `mlir`, `mlir-run`, `jit` and the demo launchers.

import "tools/flow_cli/sys.flow"
import "tools/flow_cli/toolchain.flow"
import "tools/flow_cli/tool.flow"
import "tools/flow_cli/mlir_tools.flow"
import std.process { ProcCmd, ProcResult, ProcStrs, proc_arg, proc_input, proc_now_ms }
import std.os { os_signal_watch, os_signal_take, SIGINT, SIGTERM }

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# --backend / --sanitize / --profile / --show-flags
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

export struct Parsed {
    program: string,
    backend: string
}

# flow_parse_program_backend: exits on a bad option, exports FLOW_SANITIZE,
# FLOW_PROFILE and FLOW_CPU_BACKEND.
export function parse_program_backend(args: ptr<ProcStrs>) -> Parsed {
    let mut program: string = ""
    let mut backend: string = flow_cpu_backend()
    if s_len(backend) == 0 {
        # $(flow_cpu_backend) exited 1 inside the substitution; the
        # assignment failed and `set -e` stopped the driver.
        cli_exit(1)
    }
    let mut show: bool = false
    let n: i32 = sl_len(args)
    let mut i: i32 = 0
    while i < n {
        let a: string = sl_get(args, i)
        if s_starts(a, "--backend=") {
            backend = s_from(a, 10)
        } elif s_eq(a, "--backend") {
            if i + 1 >= n or s_len(sl_get(args, i + 1)) == 0 {
                error("--backend requires c or mlir")
                cli_exit(1)
            }
            backend = sl_get(args, i + 1)
            i = i + 1
        } elif s_starts(a, "--sanitize=") {
            env_set("FLOW_SANITIZE", s_from(a, 11))
        } elif s_eq(a, "--sanitize") {
            if i + 1 >= n or s_len(sl_get(args, i + 1)) == 0 {
                error("--sanitize requires ub,asan,tsan (comma-separated)")
                cli_exit(1)
            }
            env_set("FLOW_SANITIZE", sl_get(args, i + 1))
            i = i + 1
        } elif s_starts(a, "--profile=") {
            env_set("FLOW_PROFILE", s_from(a, 10))
        } elif s_eq(a, "--profile") {
            if i + 1 >= n or s_len(sl_get(args, i + 1)) == 0 {
                error("--profile requires safety|flight")
                cli_exit(1)
            }
            env_set("FLOW_PROFILE", sl_get(args, i + 1))
            i = i + 1
        } elif s_eq(a, "--show-flags") {
            show = true
        } elif s_starts(a, "-") {
            error("Unknown option: " + a)
            cli_exit(1)
        } else {
            if s_len(program) == 0 {
                program = a
            } else {
                error("Unexpected argument: " + a)
                cli_exit(1)
            }
        }
        i = i + 1
    }
    if not (s_eq(backend, "c") or s_eq(backend, "mlir")) {
        error("Unknown backend: " + backend + " (expected c|mlir)")
        cli_exit(1)
    }
    if show {
        show_clang_flags()
        if s_len(program) == 0 {
            cli_exit(0)
        }
    }
    env_set("FLOW_CPU_BACKEND", backend)
    return Parsed { program: program, backend: backend }
}

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# run / compile / patch
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# grep -Eq 'function[[:space:]]+main' FILE
function defines_main(path: string) -> bool {
    let text: string = read_text(path)
    let mut pos: i32 = 0
    while true {
        let at: i32 = s_find(text, "function", pos)
        if at < 0 {
            return false
        }
        let mut j: i32 = at + 8
        let n: i32 = s_len(text)
        let mut spaces: i32 = 0
        while j < n and s_is_space(s_byte(text, j)) and s_byte(text, j) != 10 {
            j = j + 1
            spaces = spaces + 1
        }
        if spaces > 0 and s_starts(s_from(text, j), "main") {
            return true
        }
        pos = at + 1
    }
    return false
}

# Run an executable the way the driver's `"$exe"` line did under `set -e`:
# its status, with SIGINT/SIGTERM held off in this process meanwhile so the
# cleanup still happens.
export function run_program_binary(argv: ptr<ProcStrs>) -> i32 {
    let _a: bool = os_signal_watch(SIGINT)
    let _b: bool = os_signal_watch(SIGTERM)
    let rc: i32 = run_argv(argv)
    let _c: i32 = os_signal_take(SIGINT)
    let _d: i32 = os_signal_take(SIGTERM)
    return rc
}

export function run_program(args: ptr<ProcStrs>) -> i32 {
    let p: Parsed = parse_program_backend(args)
    let program: string = p.program
    require_flow_file(program)
    if not defines_main(program) {
        error("This Flow file does not define main() and cannot be run directly.")
        info("If it is a library or patch, use: flow patch " + program)
        return 2
    }
    check(flow_sync_program(program))
    let basename: string = path_stem(program, ".flow")
    mkdir_p_or_exit(root() + "/build")
    let run_root: string = mktemp_dir(root() + "/build/run.XXXXXX")
    if s_len(run_root) == 0 {
        error("Could not create an isolated build directory for this run.")
        return 1
    }
    on_exit_remove(run_root)
    set_build_root(run_root)
    let executable: string = run_root + "/" + basename
    if s_eq(p.backend, "mlir") {
        check(compile_program_mlir(program))
    } else {
        check(compile_program(program))
    }
    info("Running " + basename + "...")
    outln("----------------------------------------")
    let status: i32 = run_program_binary(sl_of1(executable))
    check(status)
    outln("----------------------------------------")
    success("Program finished")
    outln("Exit code: 0")
    return 0
}

# flow patch FILE: compile a patch library through a generated harness.
export function run_patch_smoke(args: ptr<ProcStrs>) -> i32 {
    let patch: string = sl_get(args, 0)
    if s_len(patch) == 0 or not is_file(patch) {
        error("Usage: flow patch <patch.flow>")
        return 1
    }
    let patch_dir: string = abs_dir(path_dirname(patch))
    let name: string = path_stem(patch, ".flow")
    let harness_dir: string = patch_dir + "/build/patches"
    let harness: string = harness_dir + "/" + name + "_smoke.flow"
    mkdir_p_or_exit(harness_dir)
    if not copy_file(patch, harness_dir + "/" + name + ".flow") {
        cli_exit(1)
    }
    let body: string = "import \"" + path_basename(patch) + "\"\n\nfunction main() -> i32 {\n    println(\"flow patch smoke: " + name + " compiled\")\n    return 0\n}\n"
    if not write_text(harness, body) {
        cli_exit(1)
    }
    return run_program(sl_of1(harness))
}

export function compile_program_cli(args: ptr<ProcStrs>) -> i32 {
    let p: Parsed = parse_program_backend(args)
    if s_eq(p.backend, "mlir") {
        return compile_program_mlir(p.program)
    }
    return compile_program(p.program)
}

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# debug
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

export function debug_program(args: ptr<ProcStrs>) -> i32 {
    let mut program: string = ""
    let mut break_spec: string = "main"
    let mut no_launch: bool = false
    let n: i32 = sl_len(args)
    let mut i: i32 = 0
    while i < n {
        let a: string = sl_get(args, i)
        if s_eq(a, "--break") {
            break_spec = sl_get(args, i + 1)
            if s_len(break_spec) == 0 {
                error("--break requires a line number or 'main'")
                cli_exit(1)
            }
            i = i + 1
        } elif s_eq(a, "--no-launch") or s_eq(a, "--keep") {
            no_launch = true
        } elif s_eq(a, "-h") or s_eq(a, "--help") {
            outln("Usage: flow debug <program.flow> [--break N|--break main] [--no-launch]")
            outln("  --break N     Break at Flow source line N (LLDB/GDB)")
            outln("  --break main  Break at main (default)")
            outln("  --no-launch   Build only; print paths and exit")
            cli_exit(0)
        } elif s_starts(a, "-") {
            error("Unknown debug option: " + a)
            cli_exit(1)
        } else {
            if s_len(program) == 0 {
                program = a
            } else {
                error("Unexpected argument: " + a)
                cli_exit(1)
            }
        }
        i = i + 1
    }
    require_flow_file(program)
    let basename: string = path_stem(program, ".flow")
    let build_dir: string = build_root()
    let c_file: string = build_dir + "/" + basename + ".debug.c"
    let exe_file: string = build_dir + "/" + basename + ".debug"
    check_deps()
    mkdir_p_or_exit(build_dir)
    info("Compiling " + program + " (debug)...")
    let abs_program: string = abs_file(program)
    let envs: ptr<ProcStrs> = sl_of2("FLOWC_DEBUG_INFO=1", "FLOWC_CGEN_FILE=" + abs_program)
    if flowc_emit_to_c_env(program, c_file, envs) != 0 {
        error("FLOW compilation failed")
        cli_exit(1)
    }
    success("FLOW to C (debug): " + path_basename(c_file))
    let saved_opt: string = env("FLOW_OPT_LEVEL")
    let had_opt: bool = env_isset("FLOW_OPT_LEVEL")
    let saved_cflags: string = env("FLOW_CFLAGS")
    let had_cflags: bool = env_isset("FLOW_CFLAGS")
    env_set("FLOW_OPT_LEVEL", "0")
    env_set("FLOW_CFLAGS", saved_cflags + " -g3 -fno-omit-frame-pointer")
    let link_rc: i32 = flowc_link_c(c_file, exe_file, program)
    restore_env("FLOW_OPT_LEVEL", had_opt, saved_opt)
    restore_env("FLOW_CFLAGS", had_cflags, saved_cflags)
    if link_rc != 0 {
        error("C compilation/linking failed")
        cli_exit(1)
    }
    success("Built debug binary: " + exe_file)
    info("Source maps: #line → " + abs_program + " (statement-level)")
    info("C mapping file: " + c_file)
    if no_launch {
        info("Skipping debugger launch (--no-launch). Run manually:")
        info("  lldb \"" + exe_file + "\"")
        return 0
    }
    let mut break_cmd: string = ""
    let mut gdb_break: string = ""
    if s_eq(break_spec, "main") {
        break_cmd = "breakpoint set --name main"
        gdb_break = "break main"
    } elif s_is_digits(break_spec) {
        break_cmd = "breakpoint set --file \"" + abs_program + "\" --line " + break_spec
        gdb_break = "break " + abs_program + ":" + break_spec
    } else {
        error("--break expects 'main' or a numeric Flow line")
        cli_exit(1)
    }
    if have("lldb") {
        info("Launching LLDB (" + break_spec + ")...")
        info("Tip: step with 'n'/'s'; 'frame variable'; 'source list'")
        let a: ptr<ProcStrs> = sl_of3("lldb", exe_file, "-o")
        sl_push(a, "settings set target.source-map . \"" + path_dirname(abs_program) + "\"")
        sl_push2(a, "-o", break_cmd)
        sl_push2(a, "-o", "run")
        return run_argv(a)
    } elif have("gdb") {
        info("Launching GDB (" + break_spec + ")...")
        let g: ptr<ProcStrs> = sl_of3("gdb", "-ex", gdb_break)
        sl_push2(g, "-ex", "run")
        sl_push(g, exe_file)
        return run_argv(g)
    }
    warning("No debugger found (lldb/gdb). Install one and run:")
    info("  lldb \"" + exe_file + "\"")
    return 0
}

export function restore_env(name: string, had: bool, value: string) {
    if had {
        env_set(name, value)
    } else {
        env_unset(name)
    }
}

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# shader
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

export function run_fill_shader(args: ptr<ProcStrs>) -> i32 {
    let program: string = sl_get(args, 0)
    let mut shader_name: string = ""
    let mut max_frames: string = "0"
    let mut width: string = "1280"
    let mut height: string = "720"
    let mut emit_only: bool = false
    let mut target: string = "metal"
    let mut layout: string = "--grid"
    let n: i32 = sl_len(args)
    let mut i: i32 = 1
    while i < n {
        let a: string = sl_get(args, i)
        if s_eq(a, "--wgsl") {
            target = "wgsl"
            emit_only = true
        } elif s_eq(a, "--name") {
            shader_name = sl_get(args, i + 1)
            i = i + 1
        } elif s_eq(a, "--frames") {
            max_frames = sl_get(args, i + 1)
            if s_len(max_frames) == 0 {
                max_frames = "0"
            }
            i = i + 1
        } elif s_eq(a, "--size") {
            let mut wh: string = sl_get(args, i + 1)
            if s_len(wh) == 0 {
                wh = "1280x720"
            }
            let x: i32 = s_rfind_byte(wh, 120)
            let x1: i32 = s_find_byte(wh, 120, 0)
            if x < 0 {
                width = wh
                height = wh
            } else {
                width = s_slice(wh, 0, x)
                height = s_from(wh, x1 + 1)
            }
            i = i + 1
        } elif s_eq(a, "--grid") {
            layout = "--grid"
        } elif s_eq(a, "--cycle") {
            layout = "--cycle"
        } elif s_eq(a, "--emit-only") {
            emit_only = true
        } else {
            error("Unknown shader option: " + a)
            cli_exit(1)
        }
        i = i + 1
    }
    info("Compiling fill-shader from " + program + "...")
    let shader_out: string = root() + "/build/shaders"
    mkdir_p_or_exit(shader_out)
    let flowc: string = flow_flowc_main()
    if s_len(flowc) == 0 {
        cli_exit(1)
    }
    let c: ptr<ProcCmd> = cmd(sl_of1(flowc))
    cmd_env(c, "FLOWC_SHADER", target)
    cmd_env(c, "FLOWC_IN", program)
    cmd_env(c, "FLOWC_OUT", shader_out)
    cmd_env(c, "FLOWC_SHADER_NAME", shader_name)
    let mut metal_path: string = capture(c)
    if last_status() != 0 {
        errln(metal_path)
        error("Shader compilation failed")
        cli_exit(1)
    }
    let lines: ptr<ProcStrs> = s_lines(metal_path)
    if sl_len(lines) > 0 {
        metal_path = sl_get(lines, sl_len(lines) - 1)
    }
    if s_eq(target, "wgsl") {
        success("FLOW → WGSL: " + metal_path)
        return 0
    }
    success("FLOW → Metal: " + path_basename(metal_path))
    let mut entries: string = metal_path
    if s_ends(metal_path, ".metal") {
        entries = s_slice(metal_path, 0, s_len(metal_path) - 6)
    }
    entries = entries + ".entries"
    if is_file(entries) {
        let count: i32 = count_newlines(read_text(entries))
        info("Gallery entries: " + s_itoa(count) + " shader(s)")
    }
    if emit_only {
        info("Emit-only: " + metal_path)
        return 0
    }
    if not s_eq(uname_s(), "Darwin") {
        error("flow shader viewer requires macOS (Metal). Use --emit-only to generate .metal.")
        cli_exit(1)
    }
    let shader_exe: string = root() + "/build/flow_shader_host"
    let shader_flow_c: string = root() + "/build/runtime_flow/shader_host.c"
    mkdir_p_or_exit(root() + "/build/runtime_flow")
    let hc: ptr<ProcCmd> = cmd(sl_of1(flowc))
    cmd_env(hc, "FLOWC_IN", root() + "/lib/runtime/shader_host.flow")
    cmd_env(hc, "FLOWC_OUT", shader_flow_c)
    if run_to_file(hc, root() + "/build/.flowc_err", true) != 0 {
        error("Failed to transpile shader_host.flow")
        errs(read_text(root() + "/build/.flowc_err"))
        cli_exit(1)
    }
    let a: ptr<ProcStrs> = sl_of3("clang", "-O2", "-fobjc-arc")
    sl_push(a, "-I" + root() + "/runtime")
    sl_push(a, root() + "/runtime/shader_host.c")
    sl_push(a, shader_flow_c)
    sl_push(a, root() + "/runtime/shader_view_metal.m")
    sl_push2(a, "-framework", "Metal")
    sl_push2(a, "-framework", "Cocoa")
    sl_push2(a, "-framework", "QuartzCore")
    sl_push2(a, "-o", shader_exe)
    if run_argv(a) != 0 {
        error("Failed to build shader host")
        cli_exit(1)
    }
    if s_eq(layout, "--grid") {
        info("Running shader GRID " + width + "x" + height + " (all at once · click cell / G / Esc)...")
    } else {
        info("Running shader CYCLE " + width + "x" + height + " (←/→ · G for grid · Esc)...")
    }
    let r: ptr<ProcStrs> = sl_of3(shader_exe, layout, metal_path)
    sl_push2(r, width, height)
    sl_push(r, max_frames)
    return run_argv(r)
}

function count_newlines(s: string) -> i32 {
    let mut n: i32 = 0
    let mut i: i32 = 0
    while i < s_len(s) {
        if s_byte(s, i) == 10 {
            n = n + 1
        }
        i = i + 1
    }
    return n
}

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# audio
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

export function compile_audio_program(program: string, backend: string) -> i32 {
    require_flow_file(program)
    let basename: string = path_stem(program, ".flow")
    let build_dir: string = build_root()
    let audio_cflags: ptr<ProcStrs> = sl_new()
    let audio_ldflags: ptr<ProcStrs> = sl_new()
    let mut audio_sources: ptr<ProcStrs> = sl_of1(root() + "/runtime/audio_miniaudio.c")
    let use_mlir: bool = s_eq(backend, "--mlir") or s_eq(env("FLOW_AUDIO_BACKEND"), "mlir")
    info("Compiling " + program + " (audio backend)...")
    mkdir_p_or_exit(build_dir)
    if use_mlir {
        check_mlir_deps()
        let ok1: bool = flow_emit_mlir(sl_of3("--lenient", program, build_dir + "/" + basename + ".mlir")) == 0
        let mut ok: bool = ok1
        if ok1 {
            ok = mlir_lower(sl_of2(build_dir + "/" + basename + ".mlir", build_dir + "/" + basename + ".ll")) == 0
        }
        if not ok {
            error("FLOW MLIR/LLVM compilation failed")
            cli_exit(1)
        }
        success("FLOW → MLIR → LLVM: " + basename + ".ll")
    } else {
        if flowc_emit_to_c(program, build_dir + "/" + basename + ".c") != 0 {
            error("FLOW compilation failed")
            cli_exit(1)
        }
        success("FLOW → C: " + basename + ".c")
    }
    if is_file(root() + "/third_party/miniaudio.h") {
        sl_push2(audio_cflags, "-I" + root() + "/third_party", "-DFLOW_AUDIO_BACKEND_MINIAUDIO")
        set_skip_audio_stub()
    } else {
        warning("miniaudio.h not found; building with Flow audio stub (no real-time audio)")
        audio_sources = sl_new()
    }
    let sys: string = uname_s()
    if s_eq(sys, "Darwin") {
        sl_push(audio_sources, root() + "/runtime/audio_gpu_metal.m")
        sl_extend(audio_ldflags, s_words("-framework CoreAudio -framework AudioToolbox -framework AudioUnit -framework Metal -framework Foundation"))
    } elif s_eq(sys, "Linux") {
        sl_push(audio_sources, root() + "/runtime/audio_gpu_metal.m")
        sl_extend(audio_ldflags, s_words("-ldl -pthread -lm"))
    }
    let mut flow_input: string = build_dir + "/" + basename + ".c"
    if use_mlir {
        flow_input = build_dir + "/" + basename + ".ll"
    }
    concurrency_flags()
    let rtf: ptr<ProcStrs> = runtime_flow_sources()
    let mut opt: string = "-O2"
    if s_eq(env("FLOW_TEST_FAST"), "1") {
        # The MLIR command golden runner uses this for large generated audio
        # graphs. Production audio builds keep the normal optimization level.
        opt = "-O0"
    }
    let a: ptr<ProcStrs> = sl_of3("clang", opt, "-fno-omit-frame-pointer")
    sl_extend(a, audio_cflags)
    sl_extend(a, py_cflags())
    sl_extend(a, conc_cflags())
    sl_push(a, flow_input)
    sl_push(a, root() + "/runtime/flow_python_embed.c")
    sl_extend(a, conc_sources())
    sl_extend(a, audio_sources)
    sl_extend(a, rtf)
    sl_extend(a, py_ldflags())
    sl_extend(a, audio_ldflags)
    sl_extend(a, conc_ldflags())
    sl_push2(a, "-o", build_dir + "/" + basename)
    let log: string = build_dir + "/" + basename + ".link.log"
    if run_err_to_file(cmd(a), log) != 0 {
        error("C compilation/linking failed")
        errs(head_of(drop_matching(read_text(log), "warning"), 20))
        cli_exit(1)
    }
    success("C → Executable: " + basename)
    success("🎧 Ready to run (audio): " + build_dir + "/" + basename)
    return 0
}

# grep -v PATTERN: the lines without it.
export function drop_matching(text: string, pattern: string) -> string {
    let lines: ptr<ProcStrs> = s_lines(text)
    let mut outs: string = ""
    let mut i: i32 = 0
    while i < sl_len(lines) {
        let l: string = sl_get(lines, i)
        if not s_contains(l, pattern) {
            outs = outs + l + "\n"
        }
        i = i + 1
    }
    return outs
}

# head -n N of a text.
export function head_of(text: string, n: i32) -> string {
    let lines: ptr<ProcStrs> = s_lines(text)
    let mut outs: string = ""
    let mut i: i32 = 0
    while i < sl_len(lines) and i < n {
        outs = outs + sl_get(lines, i) + "\n"
        i = i + 1
    }
    return outs
}

# tail -n N of a text.
export function tail_of(text: string, n: i32) -> string {
    let lines: ptr<ProcStrs> = s_lines(text)
    let mut outs: string = ""
    let mut i: i32 = sl_len(lines) - n
    if i < 0 {
        i = 0
    }
    while i < sl_len(lines) {
        outs = outs + sl_get(lines, i) + "\n"
        i = i + 1
    }
    return outs
}

export function run_audio_program(program: string, backend: string) -> i32 {
    require_flow_file(program)
    check(flow_sync_program(program))
    let basename: string = path_stem(program, ".flow")
    let executable: string = root() + "/build/" + basename
    check(compile_audio_program(program, backend))
    info("Running " + basename + " (audio)...")
    outln("----------------------------------------")
    check(run_program_binary(sl_of1(executable)))
    outln("----------------------------------------")
    success("Program finished")
    outln("Exit code: 0")
    return 0
}

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# window / gfx / record
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

export function run_window_program(program: string) -> i32 {
    require_flow_file(program)
    let basename: string = path_stem(program, ".flow")
    let build_dir: string = build_root()
    check_deps()
    if not have("pkg-config") {
        error("pkg-config is required for SDL2 linking")
        info("Install: brew install pkg-config")
        cli_exit(1)
    }
    if run_argv(sl_of3("pkg-config", "--exists", "sdl2")) != 0 {
        error("SDL2 not found (pkg-config sdl2)")
        info("Install: brew install sdl2")
        cli_exit(1)
    }
    mkdir_p_or_exit(build_dir)
    let c_file: string = build_dir + "/" + basename + ".window.c"
    let exe_file: string = build_dir + "/" + basename + ".window"
    info("Compiling " + program + " (SDL2 window)...")
    if flowc_emit_to_c(program, c_file) != 0 {
        error("FLOW compilation failed")
        cli_exit(1)
    }
    success("FLOW → C: " + path_basename(c_file))
    let sdl_cflags: string = capture(cmd(sl_of3("pkg-config", "--cflags", "sdl2")))
    check(last_status())
    let sdl_libs: string = capture(cmd(sl_of3("pkg-config", "--libs", "sdl2")))
    check(last_status())
    let rtf: ptr<ProcStrs> = runtime_flow_sources()
    let a: ptr<ProcStrs> = sl_of3("clang", "-O2", "-fno-omit-frame-pointer")
    sl_extend(a, s_words(sdl_cflags))
    sl_extend(a, py_cflags())
    sl_push(a, c_file)
    sl_push(a, root() + "/runtime/flow_python_embed.c")
    sl_push(a, root() + "/runtime/flow_rt_support.c")
    sl_push(a, root() + "/runtime/flow_rt_sysinfo.c")
    sl_extend(a, rtf)
    sl_extend(a, py_ldflags())
    sl_push2(a, "-o", exe_file)
    sl_extend(a, s_words(sdl_libs))
    sl_push(a, "-lm")
    let c: ptr<ProcCmd> = cmd(a)
    cmd_quiet_err(c)
    if run(c) != 0 {
        error("C compilation/linking failed (SDL2)")
        cli_exit(1)
    }
    success("Built: " + exe_file)
    info("Running...")
    return run_argv(sl_of1(exe_file))
}

export function run_gfx_program(program: string) -> i32 {
    require_flow_file(program)
    let basename: string = path_stem(program, ".flow")
    let build_dir: string = build_root()
    let audio_cflags: ptr<ProcStrs> = sl_new()
    let audio_sources: ptr<ProcStrs> = sl_of1(root() + "/runtime/audio_miniaudio.c")
    check_deps()
    mkdir_p_or_exit(build_dir)
    if is_file(root() + "/third_party/miniaudio.h") {
        sl_push2(audio_cflags, "-I" + root() + "/third_party", "-DFLOW_AUDIO_BACKEND_MINIAUDIO")
        set_skip_audio_stub()
    }
    let c_file: string = build_dir + "/" + basename + ".gfx.c"
    let exe_file: string = build_dir + "/" + basename + ".gfx"
    info("Compiling " + program + " (native gfx)...")
    if flowc_emit_to_c(program, c_file) != 0 {
        error("FLOW compilation failed")
        cli_exit(1)
    }
    success("FLOW → C: " + path_basename(c_file))
    concurrency_flags()
    let rtf: ptr<ProcStrs> = runtime_flow_sources()
    let link_err: string = build_dir + "/.gfx_link_err"
    let mut ok: bool = false
    let kernel: string = uname_s()
    if s_eq(kernel, "Darwin") {
        let a: ptr<ProcStrs> = sl_of3("clang", "-O2", "-fno-omit-frame-pointer")
        sl_extend(a, audio_cflags)
        sl_extend(a, py_cflags())
        sl_extend(a, conc_cflags())
        sl_push2(a, c_file, root() + "/runtime/gfx_macos.m")
        sl_extend(a, conc_sources())
        sl_extend(a, rtf)
        sl_extend(a, audio_sources)
        sl_extend(a, s_words("-framework Cocoa -framework CoreGraphics -framework QuartzCore -framework CoreText -framework CoreAudio -framework AudioToolbox -framework AudioUnit"))
        sl_extend(a, py_ldflags())
        sl_extend(a, conc_ldflags())
        sl_push2(a, "-o", exe_file)
        sl_push(a, "-lm")
        ok = run_err_to_file(cmd(a), link_err) == 0
    } else {
        let windows: bool = s_starts(kernel, "MINGW") or s_starts(kernel, "MSYS") or s_starts(kernel, "CYGWIN")
        let mut sdl_cflags: ptr<ProcStrs> = sl_new()
        let mut sdl_libs: ptr<ProcStrs> = sl_of1("-lSDL2")
        let pc_ok: bool = have("pkg-config") and quiet_ok(sl_of3("pkg-config", "--exists", "sdl2"))
        if windows and have("sdl2-config") {
            sdl_cflags = s_words(capture(cmd(sl_of2("sdl2-config", "--cflags"))))
            sdl_libs = s_words(capture(cmd(sl_of2("sdl2-config", "--libs"))))
        } elif pc_ok {
            sdl_cflags = s_words(capture(cmd(sl_of3("pkg-config", "--cflags", "sdl2"))))
            sdl_libs = s_words(capture(cmd(sl_of3("pkg-config", "--libs", "sdl2"))))
        }
        let mut backend_c: string = root() + "/runtime/gfx_linux.c"
        if windows {
            backend_c = root() + "/runtime/gfx_windows.c"
        }
        let a: ptr<ProcStrs> = sl_of3("clang", "-O2", "-fno-omit-frame-pointer")
        sl_extend(a, py_cflags())
        sl_push2(a, c_file, backend_c)
        sl_push(a, root() + "/runtime/flow_rt_support.c")
        sl_extend(a, rtf)
        sl_extend(a, sdl_cflags)
        sl_extend(a, sdl_libs)
        sl_extend(a, py_ldflags())
        sl_push2(a, "-o", exe_file)
        sl_push(a, "-lm")
        let c: ptr<ProcCmd> = cmd(a)
        cmd_quiet_err(c)
        ok = run(c) == 0
    }
    if not ok {
        error("Native gfx build failed (clang / platform graphics libs)")
        if nonempty(link_err) {
            let lines: ptr<ProcStrs> = s_lines(read_text(link_err))
            let mut i: i32 = 0
            while i < sl_len(lines) {
                errln("    " + sl_get(lines, i))
                i = i + 1
            }
        }
        cli_exit(1)
    }
    success("Built: " + exe_file)
    info("Running...")
    return run_argv(sl_of1(exe_file))
}

function quiet_ok(argv: ptr<ProcStrs>) -> bool {
    let c: ptr<ProcCmd> = cmd(argv)
    cmd_quiet(c)
    return run(c) == 0
}

# flow record PROGRAM [--frames N] [--skip N] [--out DIR] [--gif [PATH]]
#                     [--keys SPEC] [--mouse SPEC] [--fps N] [--stride N]
#                     [--width PX]
export function record_gfx_program(args: ptr<ProcStrs>) -> i32 {
    let mut program: string = ""
    let mut rec_frames: string = ""
    let mut rec_skip: string = ""
    let mut rec_dir: string = ""
    let mut rec_keys: string = ""
    let mut rec_mouse: string = ""
    let mut rec_gif: string = ""
    let mut want_gif: bool = false
    let mut gif_fps: string = ""
    let mut gif_stride: string = ""
    let mut gif_width: string = ""
    let n: i32 = sl_len(args)
    let mut i: i32 = 0
    while i < n {
        let a: string = sl_get(args, i)
        let next: string = sl_get(args, i + 1)
        if s_eq(a, "--frames") or s_eq(a, "-n") {
            rec_frames = next
            if s_len(rec_frames) == 0 {
                error("--frames needs a count, e.g. --frames 90")
                cli_exit(1)
            }
            i = i + 2
        } elif s_starts(a, "--frames=") {
            rec_frames = s_from(a, 9)
            i = i + 1
        } elif s_eq(a, "--skip") {
            rec_skip = next
            if s_len(rec_skip) == 0 {
                error("--skip needs a count, e.g. --skip 2 (keep every 2nd frame)")
                cli_exit(1)
            }
            i = i + 2
        } elif s_starts(a, "--skip=") {
            rec_skip = s_from(a, 7)
            i = i + 1
        } elif s_eq(a, "--out") or s_eq(a, "-o") {
            rec_dir = next
            if s_len(rec_dir) == 0 {
                error("--out needs a directory, e.g. --out build/frames")
                cli_exit(1)
            }
            i = i + 2
        } elif s_starts(a, "--out=") {
            rec_dir = s_from(a, 6)
            i = i + 1
        } elif s_eq(a, "--keys") {
            rec_keys = next
            i = shift2(i, n)
        } elif s_starts(a, "--keys=") {
            rec_keys = s_from(a, 7)
            i = i + 1
        } elif s_eq(a, "--mouse") {
            rec_mouse = next
            i = shift2(i, n)
        } elif s_starts(a, "--mouse=") {
            rec_mouse = s_from(a, 8)
            i = i + 1
        } elif s_eq(a, "--gif") {
            want_gif = true
            if s_len(next) > 0 and not s_starts(next, "-") {
                rec_gif = next
                i = i + 1
            }
            i = i + 1
        } elif s_starts(a, "--gif=") {
            want_gif = true
            rec_gif = s_from(a, 6)
            i = i + 1
        } elif s_eq(a, "--fps") {
            gif_fps = next
            i = shift2(i, n)
        } elif s_starts(a, "--fps=") {
            gif_fps = s_from(a, 6)
            i = i + 1
        } elif s_eq(a, "--stride") {
            gif_stride = next
            i = shift2(i, n)
        } elif s_starts(a, "--stride=") {
            gif_stride = s_from(a, 9)
            i = i + 1
        } elif s_eq(a, "--width") {
            gif_width = next
            i = shift2(i, n)
        } elif s_starts(a, "--width=") {
            gif_width = s_from(a, 8)
            i = i + 1
        } elif s_starts(a, "-") {
            error("Unknown flag for 'flow record': " + a)
            outln("  usage: flow record <program.flow> [--frames N] [--skip N] [--out DIR]")
            outln("                     [--gif [PATH]] [--keys SPEC] [--fps N] [--stride N] [--width PX]")
            cli_exit(1)
        } else {
            if s_len(program) == 0 {
                program = a
            }
            i = i + 1
        }
    }
    require_flow_file(program)
    let basename: string = path_stem(program, ".flow")
    let build_dir: string = build_root()
    if want_gif {
        if s_len(rec_gif) == 0 {
            rec_gif = build_dir + "/" + basename + ".gif"
        }
        if s_len(rec_dir) == 0 {
            rec_dir = build_dir + "/frames_" + basename
            rm_rf(rec_dir)
        }
        if s_len(rec_frames) == 0 {
            rec_frames = "120"
        }
    }
    if s_len(rec_frames) > 0 {
        env_set("FLOW_GFX_RECORD_FRAMES", rec_frames)
    }
    if s_len(rec_skip) > 0 {
        env_set("FLOW_GFX_RECORD_SKIP", rec_skip)
    }
    if s_len(rec_dir) > 0 {
        env_set("FLOW_GFX_RECORD_DIR", rec_dir)
    }
    if s_len(rec_keys) > 0 {
        env_set("FLOW_GFX_RECORD_KEYS", rec_keys)
    }
    if s_len(rec_mouse) > 0 {
        env_set("FLOW_GFX_RECORD_MOUSE", rec_mouse)
    }
    check_deps()
    mkdir_p_or_exit(build_dir)
    let c_file: string = build_dir + "/" + basename + ".record.c"
    let exe_file: string = build_dir + "/" + basename + ".record"
    info("Compiling " + program + " (headless recorder)...")
    if flowc_emit_to_c(program, c_file) != 0 {
        error("FLOW compilation failed")
        cli_exit(1)
    }
    success("FLOW → C: " + path_basename(c_file))
    let rec_logic_c: string = build_dir + "/runtime_flow/gfx_record.c"
    mkdir_p_or_exit(build_dir + "/runtime_flow")
    sink_push(SINK_NULL, SINK_NULL)
    let rrc: i32 = flowc_emit_runtime_module(root() + "/lib/runtime/gfx_record.flow", rec_logic_c)
    let _s: string = sink_pop()
    if rrc != 0 {
        error("Flow runtime module failed: gfx_record.flow")
        cli_exit(1)
    }
    success("FLOW → C: runtime_flow/gfx_record.c")
    concurrency_flags()
    let rtf: ptr<ProcStrs> = runtime_flow_sources()
    let a: ptr<ProcStrs> = sl_of3("clang", "-O2", "-fno-omit-frame-pointer")
    sl_push(a, "-Wno-error=implicit-function-declaration")
    sl_extend(a, conc_cflags())
    sl_push2(a, c_file, rec_logic_c)
    sl_push(a, root() + "/runtime/gfx_record.c")
    sl_extend(a, conc_sources())
    sl_extend(a, rtf)
    sl_extend(a, conc_ldflags())
    if s_eq(uname_s(), "Darwin") {
        sl_push2(a, "-framework", "CoreFoundation")
    }
    sl_push2(a, "-o", exe_file)
    sl_push(a, "-lm")
    if run_argv(a) != 0 {
        error("Recorder build failed")
        cli_exit(1)
    }
    success("Built: " + exe_file)
    info("Recording...")
    check(run_argv(sl_of1(exe_file)))
    if want_gif {
        info("Encoding " + rec_gif + " ...")
        let mut dir: string = rec_dir
        if s_len(dir) == 0 {
            dir = "frames"
        }
        let g: ptr<ProcStrs> = tool_argv("frames_to_gif", sl_of2(dir, rec_gif))
        if s_len(gif_fps) > 0 {
            sl_push2(g, "--fps", gif_fps)
        }
        if s_len(gif_stride) > 0 {
            sl_push2(g, "--stride", gif_stride)
        }
        if s_len(gif_width) > 0 {
            sl_push2(g, "--width", gif_width)
        }
        if run_argv(g) == 0 {
            success("GIF: " + rec_gif)
        } else {
            error("GIF encoding failed")
            cli_exit(1)
        }
    }
    return 0
}

# `shift 2` under `set -e`: with one argument left the shift fails and the
# driver stopped (status 1).
function shift2(i: i32, n: i32) -> i32 {
    if i + 2 > n {
        cli_exit(1)
    }
    return i + 2
}

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Vulkan and project demos
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

function vulkan_demo(dir_name: string, what: string, label: string, fail_label: string) -> i32 {
    let demo_dir: string = root() + "/demos/" + dir_name
    if not is_dir(demo_dir) {
        error(what + " not found: " + demo_dir)
        cli_exit(1)
    }
    if not have("make") {
        error("make is required to build the Vulkan demo")
        cli_exit(1)
    }
    if not have("pkg-config") {
        error("pkg-config is required to build the Vulkan demo")
        info("Install: brew install pkg-config")
        cli_exit(1)
    }
    if not have("glslangValidator") {
        error("glslangValidator is required to compile shaders")
        info("Install: brew install vulkan-tools")
        cli_exit(1)
    }
    if run_argv(sl_of3("pkg-config", "--exists", "vulkan")) != 0 {
        error("Vulkan loader/headers not found (pkg-config vulkan)")
        info("Install: brew install vulkan-loader vulkan-headers molten-vk")
        cli_exit(1)
    }
    if run_argv(sl_of3("pkg-config", "--exists", "glfw3")) != 0 {
        error("GLFW not found (pkg-config glfw3)")
        info("Install: brew install glfw")
        cli_exit(1)
    }
    info("Building Vulkan " + label + " demo...")
    let q: ptr<ProcCmd> = cmd(sl_of3("make", "-C", demo_dir))
    proc_arg(q, "-q")
    cmd_quiet_err(q)
    if run(q) == 0 {
        info("Build up to date (skipping rebuild).")
    } elif run_argv(sl_of3("make", "-C", demo_dir)) != 0 {
        error(fail_label + " build failed")
        cli_exit(1)
    }
    info("Running Vulkan " + label + " demo...")
    return run_vulkan_binary(demo_dir + "/" + dir_name)
}

# Run a Vulkan demo binary with the environment Homebrew's MoltenVK, Vulkan
# loader and validation layers need: the ICD and layer paths when they are
# installed, FLOW_VK_PRETTY and FLOW_VK_TRACE (default 1), and their
# libraries ahead of DYLD_LIBRARY_PATH.
function run_vulkan_binary(exe: string) -> i32 {
    let brew: string = "/opt/homebrew/opt"
    let icd: string = brew + "/molten-vk/etc/vulkan/icd.d/MoltenVK_icd.json"
    let layers: string = brew + "/vulkan-validationlayers/share/vulkan/explicit_layer.d"
    if is_file(icd) {
        env_set("VK_ICD_FILENAMES", icd)
    }
    if is_dir(layers) {
        env_set("VK_LAYER_PATH", layers)
    }
    env_set("FLOW_VK_PRETTY", env_or("FLOW_VK_PRETTY", "1"))
    env_set("FLOW_VK_TRACE", env_or("FLOW_VK_TRACE", "1"))
    let libs: ptr<ProcStrs> = sl_new()
    let candidates: ptr<ProcStrs> = sl_of3(brew + "/vulkan-validationlayers/lib", brew + "/vulkan-loader/lib", brew + "/molten-vk/lib")
    let mut i: i32 = 0
    while i < sl_len(candidates) {
        if is_dir(sl_get(candidates, i)) {
            sl_push(libs, sl_get(candidates, i))
        }
        i = i + 1
    }
    if sl_len(libs) > 0 {
        let mut dyld: string = sl_join(libs, ":")
        let old: string = env("DYLD_LIBRARY_PATH")
        if s_len(old) > 0 {
            dyld = dyld + ":" + old
        }
        env_set("DYLD_LIBRARY_PATH", dyld)
    }
    return run_argv(sl_of1(exe))
}

export function run_vulkan_demo() -> i32 {
    return vulkan_demo("vulkan_triangle", "Vulkan demo", "triangle", "Vulkan demo")
}

export function run_vulkan_demo_advanced() -> i32 {
    return vulkan_demo("vulkan_scene", "Vulkan advanced demo", "scene", "Vulkan advanced demo")
}

# flow run-native in demos/NAME, entry src/main.flow.
export function flow_demo_run_native(name: string) -> i32 {
    let demo: string = root() + "/demos/" + name
    if not is_dir(demo) {
        errln("flow: cd: " + demo + ": No such file or directory")
        return 1
    }
    return flow_pkg_native_in(demo, sl_of3("run-native", "--", demo + "/src/main.flow"))
}

export function run_ui_layout_window() -> i32 {
    return run_window_program(root() + "/demos/ui_layout_window_flow/src/main.flow")
}

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# MLIR, mlir-run, jit
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# flow mlir PROGRAM [FLAGS]: write BUILD_ROOT/<name>.mlir and print it.
export function generate_mlir(args: ptr<ProcStrs>) -> i32 {
    let mut program: string = ""
    let mut optimize: bool = false
    let mut report: bool = false
    let mut print_pipeline: bool = false
    let mut gpu: bool = false
    let mut affine: bool = false
    let mut tile_size: string = ""
    let mut tile_l2_size: string = ""
    let mut register_tiles: bool = false
    let mut aosoa_pad: bool = false
    let mut aosoa_swizzle: bool = false
    let mut spirv: bool = false
    let mut wasm32: bool = false
    let mut llvm: bool = false
    let mut jit: bool = false
    let mut shape_spec: string = ""
    let mut spirv_out: string = ""
    let mut out_path: string = ""
    let opt_flags: ptr<ProcStrs> = sl_new()
    let emit_flags: ptr<ProcStrs> = sl_new()
    let n: i32 = sl_len(args)
    let mut i: i32 = 0
    while i < n {
        let a: string = sl_get(args, i)
        if s_eq(a, "--optimize") {
            optimize = true
        } elif s_eq(a, "--opt-level") {
            sl_push2(opt_flags, a, sl_get(args, i + 1))
            i = i + 1
        } elif s_starts(a, "--opt-level=") {
            sl_push2(opt_flags, "--opt-level", s_from(a, 12))
        } elif s_eq(a, "--no-vectorization") or s_eq(a, "--loop-fusion") or s_eq(a, "--no-loop-fusion") or s_eq(a, "--no-mem2reg") or s_eq(a, "--no-sccp") or s_eq(a, "--no-licm") or s_eq(a, "--no-cse") or s_eq(a, "--no-dce") or s_eq(a, "--no-inline") or s_eq(a, "--no-aosoa") {
            sl_push(opt_flags, a)
        } elif s_eq(a, "--opt-report") {
            report = true
        } elif s_eq(a, "--print-pass-pipeline") {
            print_pipeline = true
        } elif s_eq(a, "--mlir-gpu") {
            gpu = true
        } elif s_eq(a, "--affine") {
            affine = true
        } elif s_eq(a, "--tile-size") {
            if i + 1 >= n {
                error("flow mlir: --tile-size requires a value")
                cli_exit(2)
            }
            affine = true
            tile_size = sl_get(args, i + 1)
            i = i + 1
        } elif s_starts(a, "--tile-size=") {
            affine = true
            tile_size = s_from(a, 12)
            if s_len(tile_size) == 0 {
                error("flow mlir: --tile-size requires a value")
                cli_exit(2)
            }
        } elif s_eq(a, "--tile-l2-size") {
            if i + 1 >= n {
                error("flow mlir: --tile-l2-size requires a value")
                cli_exit(2)
            }
            affine = true
            tile_l2_size = sl_get(args, i + 1)
            i = i + 1
        } elif s_starts(a, "--tile-l2-size=") {
            affine = true
            tile_l2_size = s_from(a, 15)
            if s_len(tile_l2_size) == 0 {
                error("flow mlir: --tile-l2-size requires a value")
                cli_exit(2)
            }
        } elif s_eq(a, "--register-tiles") {
            register_tiles = true
        } elif s_eq(a, "--aosoa-pad") {
            aosoa_pad = true
        } elif s_eq(a, "--aosoa-swizzle") {
            aosoa_swizzle = true
        } elif s_eq(a, "--emit-spirv") {
            spirv = true
        } elif s_eq(a, "--spirv-out") {
            spirv_out = sl_get(args, i + 1)
            i = i + 1
        } elif s_eq(a, "--wasm32") {
            wasm32 = true
        } elif s_eq(a, "--llvm") {
            llvm = true
        } elif s_starts(a, "--shape-spec=") {
            shape_spec = s_from(a, 13)
        } elif s_eq(a, "--jit") or s_eq(a, "--hot-reload") {
            jit = true
        } elif s_eq(a, "-o") or s_eq(a, "--output") {
            out_path = sl_get(args, i + 1)
            i = i + 1
        } elif s_eq(a, "--mode") {
            i = i + 1
        } elif s_eq(a, "--lenient") {
            sl_push(emit_flags, "--lenient")
        } elif s_eq(a, "--mlir") or s_eq(a, "--strict") or s_eq(a, "--verify") or s_eq(a, "--strict-effects") or s_eq(a, "--module-info") or s_eq(a, "--validate-imports") or s_starts(a, "--mode=") {
            let _skip: i32 = 0
        } elif s_eq(a, "--debug-info") {
            warning("--debug-info: the Flow MLIR emitter writes no DWARF debug info")
        } elif s_eq(a, "--gpu") or s_eq(a, "--gpu-backend") or s_starts(a, "--gpu-backend=") {
            error("flow mlir: " + a + " (the Python CUDA/OpenCL integration) is retired; use --mlir-gpu, flow gpu, or --gpu on flow run")
            cli_exit(2)
        } elif s_starts(a, "-") {
            error("flow mlir: unknown option " + a)
            cli_exit(2)
        } else {
            if s_len(program) == 0 {
                program = a
            } else {
                error("flow mlir: unexpected argument " + a)
                cli_exit(2)
            }
        }
        i = i + 1
    }
    if print_pipeline {
        let pp: ptr<ProcStrs> = sl_of1("--print-pass-pipeline")
        sl_extend(pp, opt_flags)
        return mlir_optimize(pp)
    }
    if s_len(program) == 0 or not is_file(program) {
        error("Program not found: " + program)
        cli_exit(1)
    }
    if jit {
        return run_flow_jit(program, shape_spec)
    }
    let basename: string = path_stem(program, ".flow")
    let build_dir: string = build_root()
    let mlir_file: string = build_dir + "/" + basename + ".mlir"
    mkdir_p_or_exit(build_dir)
    check_mlir_deps()
    if gpu {
        sl_push(emit_flags, "--gpu")
    }
    if affine {
        sl_push(emit_flags, "--affine")
    }
    if s_len(tile_size) > 0 {
        sl_push(emit_flags, "--tile-size=" + tile_size)
    }
    if s_len(tile_l2_size) > 0 {
        sl_push(emit_flags, "--tile-l2-size=" + tile_l2_size)
    }
    if register_tiles {
        sl_push(emit_flags, "--register-tiles")
    }
    if aosoa_pad {
        sl_push(emit_flags, "--aosoa-pad")
    }
    if aosoa_swizzle {
        sl_push(emit_flags, "--aosoa-swizzle")
    }
    if wasm32 {
        sl_push(emit_flags, "--wasm32")
    }
    if s_len(shape_spec) > 0 {
        sl_push(emit_flags, "--shape-spec=" + shape_spec)
    }
    sl_push2(emit_flags, program, mlir_file)
    if flow_emit_mlir(emit_flags) != 0 {
        error("MLIR generation failed")
        cli_exit(1)
    }
    if optimize {
        let o: ptr<ProcStrs> = sl_copy(opt_flags)
        if report {
            sl_push(o, "--opt-report")
        }
        sl_push2(o, mlir_file, mlir_file)
        if mlir_optimize(o) != 0 {
            errln("MLIR optimization failed")
            error("MLIR generation failed")
            cli_exit(1)
        }
    }
    if llvm {
        if mlir_lower(sl_of2(mlir_file, mlir_file + ".ll")) != 0 {
            errln("LLVM IR generation failed")
            error("MLIR generation failed")
            cli_exit(1)
        }
        let _mv: bool = move_file(mlir_file + ".ll", mlir_file)
    }
    if spirv {
        if s_len(spirv_out) == 0 {
            spirv_out = "build/" + basename + ".spv"
        }
        sink_push(SINK_BUF, SINK_SAME)
        let src: i32 = mlir_spirv(sl_of3("spirv", mlir_file, spirv_out))
        let spirv_err: string = s_chomp_all(sink_pop())
        if src != 0 {
            errln("SPIR-V generation failed: " + spirv_err)
            error("MLIR generation failed")
            cli_exit(1)
        }
        errln("Generated SPIR-V: " + spirv_out)
    }
    if s_len(out_path) > 0 {
        mkdir_p_or_exit(path_dirname(out_path))
        let _cp: bool = copy_file(mlir_file, out_path)
    }
    success("Generated MLIR: " + mlir_file)
    outln("----------------------------------------")
    out(read_text(mlir_file))
    outln("----------------------------------------")
    return 0
}

export struct JITPhaseTimings {
    emit_ms: i64,
    optimize_ms: i64,
    lower_ms: i64,
    link_ms: i64,
    run_ms: i64,
}

# flow jit PROGRAM: emit, optimize, lower, link and run natively.
export function run_flow_jit(program: string, shape_spec: string) -> i32 {
    let name: string = path_basename(program)
    let raw: bool = s_eq(env_or("FLOW_JIT_RAW", "0"), "1")

    let cache_dir: string = env_or("XDG_CACHE_HOME", env("HOME") + "/.cache") + "/flow/jit"
    mkdir_p_or_exit(cache_dir)
    let key: string = cksum_key(sl_of1(program))
    let cached_exe: string = cache_dir + "/" + key + "_" + name + ".exe"

    # A shape spec changes the emitted MLIR, so do not reuse a cache entry
    # keyed only on the source file.
    let is_cached: bool = s_len(shape_spec) == 0 and is_exec(cached_exe) and not deps_newer(program, path_dirname(program), cached_exe)
    let mut timings: JITPhaseTimings = JITPhaseTimings { emit_ms: 0, optimize_ms: 0, lower_ms: 0, link_ms: 0, run_ms: 0 }

    let mut rc: i32 = 0
    if is_cached {
        if not raw {
            outln("🔥 JIT running cached " + name + "...")
        }
        let timeout_s: string = env_or("FLOW_JIT_TIMEOUT", "300")
        let has_timeout: bool = have("timeout")
        let mut rargv: ptr<ProcStrs> = sl_of1(cached_exe)
        if has_timeout {
            rargv = sl_of3("timeout", timeout_s, cached_exe)
        }
        let pc: ptr<ProcCmd> = cmd(rargv)
        let t4: i64 = proc_now_ms()
        rc = run(pc)
        timings.run_ms = proc_now_ms() - t4

        if rc == 124 and has_timeout {
            outln("❌ JIT execution timed out after " + timeout_s + "s")
            rc = 0 - 1
        } elif rc > 128 {
            rc = 128 - rc
        }

        if not jit_is_crash(rc) {
            if not raw {
                if rc != 0 {
                    outln("❌ JIT finished with exit code: " + s_itoa(rc))
                } else {
                    outln("✅ JIT finished with exit code: 0")
                }
            }
        } else {
            outln("❌ JIT crashed (exit " + s_itoa(rc) + "): a fault in the native code")
        }
    } else {
        if not raw {
            outln("🔥 JIT compiling " + name + "...")
        }
        let work: string = mktemp_dir(tmp_base() + "/flow_jit_XXXXXX")
        if s_len(work) == 0 {
            return 1
        }
        rc = flow_jit_once(program, work, cached_exe, &timings, shape_spec)
        rm_rf(work)
    }

    if not raw {
        outln("== timings ==")
        if not is_cached {
            outln("  emit:     " + s_itoa(timings.emit_ms as i32) + " ms")
            outln("  optimize: " + s_itoa(timings.optimize_ms as i32) + " ms")
            outln("  lower:    " + s_itoa(timings.lower_ms as i32) + " ms")
            outln("  link:     " + s_itoa(timings.link_ms as i32) + " ms")
        } else {
            outln("  (warm cache, compilation skipped)")
        }
        outln("  run:      " + s_itoa(timings.run_ms as i32) + " ms")
    }

    if s_eq(env_or("FLOW_JIT_RAW", "0"), "1") {
        return rc & 255
    }
    if rc != 0 {
        return 1
    }
    return 0
}

function jit_is_crash(code: i32) -> bool {
    return code < 0 or code == 134 or code == 138 or code == 139
}

function flow_jit_once(program: string, work: string, cached_exe: string, timings: ptr<JITPhaseTimings>, shape_spec: string) -> i32 {
    sink_push(SINK_FD, SINK_BUF)
    let t0: i64 = proc_now_ms()
    let eargs: ptr<ProcStrs> = sl_of1("--jit")
    if s_len(shape_spec) > 0 {
        let mut spec: string = shape_spec
        if s_starts(spec, "--shape-spec=") {
            spec = s_from(spec, 13)
        }
        sl_push(eargs, "--shape-spec=" + spec)
    }
    sl_push2(eargs, program, work + "/jit_module.mlir")
    let erc: i32 = flow_emit_mlir(eargs)
    timings[0].emit_ms = proc_now_ms() - t0
    let _eo: string = sink_pop()
    if erc != 0 {
        errs(sink_err())
        outln("❌ JIT error: MLIR generation failed for " + path_basename(program))
        return 1
    }

    let is_small: bool = file_size(program) < 4096
    let o: ptr<ProcStrs> = sl_new()
    if is_small {
        sl_push2(o, "--opt-level", "O0")
    } else {
        sl_push2(o, "--opt-level", "O2")
    }
    sl_push2(o, work + "/jit_module.mlir", work + "/jit_module.mlir")

    let t1: i64 = proc_now_ms()
    if mlir_optimize(o) != 0 {
        errln("MLIR optimization failed")
        return 1
    }
    timings[0].optimize_ms = proc_now_ms() - t1
    let mut ok: bool = true
    sink_push(SINK_FD, SINK_BUF)
    let t2: i64 = proc_now_ms()
    let lrc: i32 = mlir_lower(sl_of2(work + "/jit_module.mlir", work + "/jit_module.ll"))
    timings[0].lower_ms = proc_now_ms() - t2
    let _lo: string = sink_pop()
    if lrc != 0 {
        outln("MLIR lowering (mlir-opt) failed: " + s_chomp_all(sink_err()))
        ok = false
    }
    let asan_env: string = env("FLOW_JIT_ASAN")
    let lower: string = s_lower(asan_env)
    let asan_off: bool = s_eq(lower, "0") or s_eq(lower, "false") or s_eq(lower, "no") or s_eq(lower, "off")
    let attempts: ptr<ProcStrs> = sl_new()
    if s_len(asan_env) > 0 and asan_off {
        sl_push2(attempts, "fast", "asan")
    } elif s_len(asan_env) > 0 or s_eq(uname_s(), "Darwin") {
        sl_push(attempts, "asan")
    } else {
        sl_push2(attempts, "fast", "asan")
    }
    let link_env: string = s_lower(env_or("FLOW_JIT_LINK_RUNTIME", "1"))
    let link_rt: bool = not (s_eq(link_env, "0") or s_eq(link_env, "false") or s_eq(link_env, "no") or s_eq(link_env, "off") or s_len(link_env) == 0)
    let rt_args: ptr<ProcStrs> = sl_new()
    if link_rt {
        concurrency_flags()
        let rtf: ptr<ProcStrs> = runtime_flow_sources()
        gpu_link_flags()
        sl_extend(rt_args, conc_cflags())
        sl_extend(rt_args, conc_sources())
        sl_extend(rt_args, rtf)
        sl_extend(rt_args, gpu_sources())
        sl_extend(rt_args, gpu_ldflags())
        sl_extend(rt_args, conc_ldflags())
    }
    let timeout_s: string = env_or("FLOW_JIT_TIMEOUT", "300")
    let mut result: string = ""
    let n: i32 = sl_len(attempts)
    let mut idx: i32 = 0
    if ok {
        let mut k: i32 = 0
        while k < n {
            let kind: string = sl_get(attempts, k)
            idx = idx + 1
            k = k + 1
            let a: ptr<ProcStrs> = sl_of1("clang")
            if s_eq(kind, "asan") {
                sl_extend(a, s_words("-fsanitize=address -g -O2 -fno-omit-frame-pointer"))
            } else {
                sl_push(a, "-O2")
            }
            let exe: string = work + "/jit_module_" + s_itoa(idx)
            sl_push2(a, "-Wno-override-module", work + "/jit_module.ll")
            sl_extend(a, rt_args)
            sl_push2(a, "-o", exe)
            sl_push(a, "-lm")
            let cc: ptr<ProcCmd> = cmd(a)
            cmd_no_stdin(cc)
            let t3: i64 = proc_now_ms()
            if run_err_to_file(cc, work + "/cc.err") != 0 {
                outln("LLVM executable build failed: " + s_chomp_all(read_text(work + "/cc.err")))
                continue
            }
            timings[0].link_ms = proc_now_ms() - t3
            let has_timeout: bool = have("timeout")
            let mut rargv: ptr<ProcStrs> = sl_of1(exe)
            if has_timeout {
                rargv = sl_of3("timeout", timeout_s, exe)
            }
            let rc: ptr<ProcCmd> = cmd(rargv)
            cmd_no_stdin(rc)
            let t4: i64 = proc_now_ms()
            let mut code: i32 = run(rc)
            timings[0].run_ms = proc_now_ms() - t4
            if code == 124 and has_timeout {
                outln("❌ JIT execution timed out after " + timeout_s + "s")
                code = 0 - 1
            } elif code > 128 {
                code = 128 - code
            }
            result = s_itoa(code)
            if not jit_is_crash(code) {
                let _cp: bool = copy_file(exe, cached_exe)
                let _sm: bool = set_mode(cached_exe, 493) # 0755
                break
            }
            if idx < n {
                outln("⚠️  JIT native crash (exit " + s_itoa(code) + "); retrying with ASAN executable...")
                continue
            }
            outln("❌ JIT native crash (exit " + s_itoa(code) + ") after all attempts")
        }
    }
    if s_len(result) == 0 {
        outln("❌ JIT execution failed (see errors above)")
        outln("   Requires: mlir-opt, mlir-translate, clang on PATH")
        outln("   macOS: brew install llvm && export PATH=\"$(brew --prefix llvm)/bin:$PATH\"")
        return 1
    }
    let code: i32 = s_atoi(result, 0)
    if jit_is_crash(code) {
        outln("❌ JIT crashed (exit " + result + "): a fault in the native code")
        outln("   Usually arm64 aggregate-return stack aliasing in MLIR codegen.")
        outln("   ASAN retry should have run automatically; unset FLOW_JIT_ASAN=0 to prefer ASAN.")
        return code
    }
    if not s_eq(env_or("FLOW_JIT_RAW", "0"), "1") {
        if code != 0 {
            outln("❌ JIT finished with exit code: " + result)
        } else {
            outln("✅ JIT finished with exit code: " + result)
        }
    }
    return code
}

# Lower MLIR to an object with mlir-opt | mlir-translate | llc and link it
# with the Flow runtime (flow mlir-run, flow ml bench).
export function mlir_lower_and_link(mlir_file: string, obj_file: string, exe_file: string, opt_level: string) -> i32 {
    info("Lowering MLIR to LLVM IR...")
    let lp: string = llvm_path()
    # mlir-opt ... | mlir-translate --mlir-to-llvmir | llc ... (pipefail):
    # each stage's output is the next one's input.
    let opt: ptr<ProcStrs> = sl_of2(lp + "/mlir-opt", mlir_file)
    sl_extend(opt, s_words("--convert-vector-to-scf --convert-scf-to-cf --memref-expand --convert-vector-to-llvm --convert-arith-to-llvm --convert-index-to-llvm --convert-cf-to-llvm --convert-func-to-llvm --finalize-memref-to-llvm --reconcile-unrealized-casts"))
    let lowered: string = capture_raw(cmd(opt))
    let s1: i32 = last_status()
    let tr: ptr<ProcCmd> = cmd(sl_of2(lp + "/mlir-translate", "--mlir-to-llvmir"))
    proc_input(tr, lowered)
    let ir: string = capture_raw(tr)
    let s2: i32 = last_status()
    let llc: ptr<ProcStrs> = sl_of3(lp + "/llc", "-O" + opt_level, "-relocation-model=pic")
    sl_push2(llc, "-filetype=obj", "-o")
    sl_push(llc, obj_file)
    let lc: ptr<ProcCmd> = cmd(llc)
    proc_input(lc, ir)
    let s3: i32 = run(lc)
    if s1 != 0 or s2 != 0 or s3 != 0 {
        error("MLIR to LLVM lowering failed")
        return 1
    }
    success("MLIR → LLVM IR → Object")
    info("Linking executable (Flow runtime)...")
    concurrency_flags()
    let rtf: ptr<ProcStrs> = runtime_flow_sources()
    gpu_link_flags()
    let a: ptr<ProcStrs> = sl_of3("clang", "-O" + opt_level, "-fno-omit-frame-pointer")
    sl_extend(a, conc_cflags())
    sl_push(a, obj_file)
    sl_push(a, root() + "/runtime/flow_python_embed.c")
    sl_extend(a, conc_sources())
    sl_extend(a, rtf)
    sl_extend(a, gpu_sources())
    sl_extend(a, gpu_ldflags())
    sl_extend(a, conc_ldflags())
    sl_push2(a, "-lm", "-o")
    sl_push(a, exe_file)
    let log: string = exe_file + ".link.log"
    if run_err_to_file(cmd(a), log) != 0 {
        error("Linking failed")
        errs(head_of(drop_matching(read_text(log), "warning"), 20))
        return 1
    }
    success("Built: " + exe_file)
    return 0
}
